@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000

### Run in order using the VS Code REST Client extension.
### This file uses fictional data. If this email exists, delete it or change it.
# @name create
POST {{baseUrl}}/students
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Request Demo",
  "date_of_birth": "2006-04-12",
  "email": "request.demo@example.com",
  "course": "Python",
  "enrollment_date": "2026-01-10"
}

### List / filter
GET {{baseUrl}}/students?course=Python&born_after=2005-12-31&limit=20&offset=0

### Read created student
GET {{baseUrl}}/students/{{create.response.body.$.student_id}}

### Partial update
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/students/{{create.response.body.$.student_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"course": "Data Science"}

### Full replacement
PUT {{baseUrl}}/students/{{create.response.body.$.student_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Request Demo Updated",
  "date_of_birth": "2006-04-12",
  "email": "request.demo@example.com",
  "course": "Python",
  "enrollment_date": "2026-01-10"
}

### Grounded question without Ollama
POST {{baseUrl}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "List students born after 2005", "use_ai": false}

### Optional Ollama commentary (enable and run Ollama first)
POST {{baseUrl}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "How many students are there?", "use_ai": true}

### Delete created student
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/students/{{create.response.body.$.student_id}}

### Expected 404 after deletion
GET {{baseUrl}}/students/{{create.response.body.$.student_id}}
